        <section id="cogitatio-gregis">
            <div class="section-header">
                <h2 class="section-title">cogitatio gregis</h2>
                <div class="section-subheading">Group Reflection</div>
            </div>
            <div class="reflection-card">
                <p>
                    While our personal confessions remain sacred and private between God and us, the struggles we face are profoundly shared. Putting this book together highlighted a clear truth. We came to understand how easily high schoolers can feel isolated, presenting polished exteriors while silently grappling with daily anxieties about the future, moments of uncertainty, and the pressure to excel.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Reflecting on St. Augustine’s journey taught us that being vulnerable before God is not a sign of weakness, but rather the beginning of grace. Even while honoring the confidentiality of our individual paths, the act of writing our testimonies fostered a silent, powerful connection among us. We realized that our restless hearts are not broken; they are merely in search of truth, purpose, and peace. Through this project, we learned to see our classmates with greater empathy, knowing that behind every face is a soul learning to trust God’s timing and love.
                </p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="votum-ultimum">
            <div class="section-header">
                <h2 class="section-title">Votum Ultimum</h2>
                <div class="section-subheading">Final Prayer</div>
            </div>
            <div class="prayer-card">
                <p>
                    Lord God, we come before You as young confessors, bringing our honest stories, our unfinished paths, and our deepest hopes. Thank You for meeting us in our stumbles, holding us steady in our doubts, and reminding us that Your love never runs out. Standing together, we vow to live out the resolutions formed during this journey by committing to embrace authenticity, choosing truth and honesty over pretense even when it feels uncomfortable. We promise to extend unconditional grace, offering patience, forgiveness, and kindness to those around us, knowing that everyone carries unseen battles. Finally, we vow to seek true rest, reminding ourselves daily of St. Augustine's realization that our restless desires will never be satisfied by external success or perfection, but only in Your peace. As we step forward toward what lies ahead, anchor our steps in faith, guide our decisions with wisdom, and let our lives always reflect the quiet echoes of Your grace.
                </p>
                <div class="amen-text">Amen.</div>
            </div>
        </section>
